  "worked_solution": "Let's add the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ to the plot.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14255079/assets/d5a7d0514b53a552fe1fc0f4b778583ee1dc313245161769537a2c0b06a3e1d4.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$\n\n- Then, shift it by $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ units **right.**\n\nTherefore, the given graph is $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$",
